WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.410
On the island of Java stands Borobudur,
a vast Buddhist monument built around

2
00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:07.040
the year 800.

3
00:00:07.090 --> 00:00:09.890
Yet the teaching it honors began far away,

4
00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:11.780
in northern South Asia.

5
00:00:11.830 --> 00:00:14.590
Buddhist tradition says
a prince saw old age,

6
00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:18.940
sickness and death, and left
home to understand suffering.

7
00:00:18.990 --> 00:00:23.250
So how did one teacher's answer to
suffering spread all the way to Japan,

8
00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:25.200
Tibet and Java?

9
00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:28.580
In this mission, you'll
learn the Four Noble Truths:

10
00:00:28.630 --> 00:00:31.630
a diagnosis of suffering, and a cure.

11
00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:36.500
Then you'll compare three branches of
Buddhism and see where each one took root.

12
00:00:36.550 --> 00:00:41.800
Your mission: find out how one teacher's
answer to suffering traveled across Asia.
